    <section id="cs-top">
        <h1>Orion and Nexus: the AI operating layer</h1>
        <h2>How a growing collection of AI tools became a platform the whole agency could use.</h2>
        <figure class="story-illustration case-header-visual">
            <%= image_tag "nexus-branching-options.jpg", alt: "Hand-drawn source of ideas branching into different product directions" %>
        </figure>
        <p class="lede">At Mod Op, I led product and technical direction for Nexus, the platform underneath our AI work. It began with a practical need inside Mod Heat: the product had to understand the person using it, the organization they belonged to, and the brand context behind a signal. From there, Nexus grew into a shared home for identity, permissions, knowledge, and agents. Nexus Chat put those capabilities in front of the whole agency, and Orion later gave the portfolio a common story. The work sat inside a $10M AI investment at a roughly 500-person organization.</p>
        <p class="lede">Mod Op's public materials use the names Mod Engine, Mod Chat, and, from July 2026, Orion. Inside the team the platform was Nexus and its workspace was Nexus Chat, and those are the names I use here.</p>
    </section>

    <nav class="case-nav" aria-label="Nexus case study chapters">
        <a href="#cs-foundation"><span>01</span> Foundation</a>
        <a href="#cs-context"><span>02</span> Context</a>
